    fix: repo-root .tmp_* scratch files no longer red the Tier-1 lint arm. Addresses AUG-049.
    
    Untracked scratch scripts (.tmp_*.py) in the repo root turned the Tier-1 lint
    arm red on a clean tree — proven 09-23 on fb2bff77/AUG-035 where the step failed
    with E401 pointing at .tmp_tick_board.py and .tmp_tick_worker_probe.py while the
    committed tree at HEAD linted clean. The built-in lint arm selects files itself
    (it ignores lint_command), so it picked up litter .gitignore did not cover.
    
    - .gitignore: add repo-root .tmp_* rule (ruff respects gitignore, so
      `ruff check .` stays clean even when litter exists — verified with a probe
      file before and after the rule).
    - README: document the convention — scratch scripts go under /tmp, never the
      workdir; the gitignore rule is the seatbelt, the convention is the fix.
    
    Verified: ruff check . with a staged-style .tmp_ probe = "All checks passed!";
    git check-ignore proves the rule matches; committed tree unchanged.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
